  "scope": "Ordinary MOL2 -> CJSON selected-field projection and refusal of ambiguous charge data. 27 projection inputs, 12 ambiguous-charge controls, 9 one-record invalid/out-of-domain controls. Development packet, not a holdout, toolkit-wide/speed/release/complete-chemistry claim.",
  "compatibility": "Python rejects overrides and uses bounded 10000-atom projection. NO_CHARGES raw zero placeholders are omitted as explicitly unassigned; USER_CHARGES signed zeros are assigned values and retained. The existing strict/allow_loss policies remain available; selected projection is not strict preservation.",
  "oracle": "Declared source-ID-to-row graph, N.4 projected formal charge, coordinate decimal tokens, name, partial values/absence and method/absence. No stereo/hydrogen equivalence. All scored sources have sparse IDs; sequential-ID diagnostics retained separately. Nonempty competitor text is not necessarily valid JSON. Multiple source records are out of domain for one-record APIs, not universally invalid MOL2.",
